  era: "Section 25 \xB7 Gandhian Era \xB7 1917 \u2013 1947"
  title: Non-Cooperation Movement
  text: Launched in 1920 after the Jallianwala Bagh massacre and alongside the Khilafat movement, it urged Indians to boycott foreign goods, courts, schools and titles. Gandhi called it off in 1922 after the violence at Chauri Chaura.
